@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor #FAF6EB
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam defaultFontColor #291B1D
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #BA3143
skinparam activityBackgroundColor white
skinparam activityBorderColor #BA3143
skinparam activityDiamondBackgroundColor #D8F24B
skinparam activityDiamondBorderColor #291B1D
skinparam classBackgroundColor white
skinparam classBorderColor #BA3143
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam sequenceParticipantBackgroundColor white
skinparam sequenceParticipantBorderColor #BA3143
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor #291B1D
skinparam sequenceGroupBackgroundColor white
skinparam sequenceGroupBorderColor #BA3143
skinparam rectangleBackgroundColor white
skinparam rectangleBorderColor #BA3143
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFDF6
skinparam noteBorderColor #BA3143
title Open a personal race recap — main requirement FR-01
hide footbox
autonumber
actor Runner
boundary "Recap page" as UI
control "Recap service\n(proposed responsibility)" as Service
database "Prototype database\n(Supabase)" as DB
control "Result calculations\n(proposed responsibility)" as Logic
Runner -> UI : Select runner / enter BIB
UI -> Service : Request recap(selected identifier)
Service -> DB : Find runner, category, result and splits
DB --> Service : Matching baseline records or no match
alt Runner or result unavailable
  Service --> UI : Result-unavailable state
  UI --> Runner : Explain; offer retry / runner selection
else Matching runner and result
  alt Known DNF
    Service -> Logic : Prepare DNF summary(recorded data)
    Logic --> Service : DNF; no finish time or finish pace
  else Valid finisher timing
    Service -> Logic : Prepare timing, pace, ranks and split insights
    note right of Logic
      Elapsed = finish minus start
      Pace = elapsed / category distance
      Rank and split policies: OD-02 / OD-03
    end note
    Logic --> Service : Finisher summary from recorded data
  else Unresolved DNS or invalid timing
    Service --> UI : Result-unavailable / pending policy state
    UI --> Runner : No invented finish or DNF label
    note over UI,Service : Final lifecycle behavior remains OD-01
  end
  opt A valid finisher or known-DNF recap can be prepared
    Service -> DB : Read stored optional metrics and photos for runner / BIB
    DB --> Service : Available records; empty collections allowed
    Service -> Service : Combine runner-specific summary and optional data
    Service --> UI : Recap model; gallery or no-photo state
    UI --> Runner : Render personal recap
  end
end
note over UI,DB
Opening a recap does not initiate Strava OAuth or require a live Strava request.
Optional connection is a separate runner action (FR-08–FR-11).
Responsibilities describe a proposed design, not verified code classes.
end note
@enduml
